WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.374
Phrase Bank.

2
00:00:01.654 --> 00:00:04.107
From the Reference part of the Soft Skill Playbook.

3
00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:06.881
The key idea.

4
00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:12.068
Learn 5 phrases a week and use each one at least twice in real conversations.

5
00:00:12.348 --> 00:00:16.465
Within 3 months you'll have 60 phrases you can say without thinking.

6
00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:18.711
Agreeing.

7
00:00:18.991 --> 00:00:20.058
That makes sense.

8
00:00:20.338 --> 00:00:21.853
I'm fully on board with that.

9
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.007
Good point.

10
00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:24.397
Let's go with it.

11
00:00:24.677 --> 00:00:26.597
I agree, and I'd add one thing...

12
00:00:27.947 --> 00:00:29.355
Disagreeing politely.

13
00:00:29.635 --> 00:00:31.149
I see it a bit differently.

14
00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:33.179
I'm not sure that'll work, because...

15
00:00:33.459 --> 00:00:35.272
Can I offer another perspective?

16
00:00:35.552 --> 00:00:37.067
I understand the reasoning.

17
00:00:37.347 --> 00:00:38.520
My concern is...

18
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.973
What if we tried...?

19
00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:42.646
Asking for clarity.

20
00:00:42.926 --> 00:00:44.462
Could you walk me through that again?

21
00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:46.555
What do you mean by 'scalable' here?

22
00:00:46.835 --> 00:00:49.225
Just to make sure I understand: you're saying...?

23
00:00:49.505 --> 00:00:50.998
Could you give me an example?

24
00:00:52.348 --> 00:00:53.329
Buying time.

25
00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:54.612
Good question.

26
00:00:54.892 --> 00:00:56.129
Let me think about that.

27
00:00:56.409 --> 00:00:58.735
I'd like to check the data before I answer.

28
00:00:59.015 --> 00:01:00.892
Can I get back to you by end of day?

29
00:01:02.242 --> 00:01:03.095
Ownership.

30
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:04.591
I'll take care of it.

31
00:01:04.871 --> 00:01:05.831
That's on me.

32
00:01:06.111 --> 00:01:07.434
Here's how I'll fix it.

33
00:01:07.714 --> 00:01:08.994
I'll own the follow-up.

34
00:01:09.274 --> 00:01:10.746
You can count on me for this.

35
00:01:12.096 --> 00:01:13.867
Apologising (when you should).

36
00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:15.320
I apologise.

37
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.560
I missed that.

38
00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.845
You're right, I should have flagged it earlier.

39
00:01:19.125 --> 00:01:20.533
Sorry for the confusion.

40
00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.243
Here's the correct version.

41
00:01:22.523 --> 00:01:24.315
Instead of over-apologising:

42
00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:28.520
Thanks for your patience, Thanks for catching that, Appreciate you waiting.

43
00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:30.979
Asking for help.

44
00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:32.966
Could I get your input on something?

45
00:01:33.246 --> 00:01:35.422
Do you have 10 minutes to look at this with me?

46
00:01:35.702 --> 00:01:37.153
I've tried X and Y.

47
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:38.905
What would you suggest next?

48
00:01:40.255 --> 00:01:41.215
Saying no.

49
00:01:41.495 --> 00:01:44.161
I'd love to help, but I'm at capacity this week.

50
00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:45.401
Not right now.

51
00:01:45.681 --> 00:01:47.260
Could we revisit next sprint?

52
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.183
I can do X, but not Y.

53
00:01:49.463 --> 00:01:52.087
Which should I deprioritise to make room for this?

54
00:01:53.437 --> 00:01:54.482
Giving praise.

55
00:01:54.762 --> 00:01:56.191
Great work on the release.

56
00:01:56.471 --> 00:01:58.455
The rollback plan was really thorough.

57
00:01:58.735 --> 00:02:00.527
Thank you, you saved us hours.

58
00:02:00.807 --> 00:02:03.367
I really liked how you explained that to the client.

59
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:05.549
Closing.

60
00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:07.600
Let's summarise what we've agreed.

61
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.288
Who's doing what by when?

62
00:02:09.568 --> 00:02:11.040
I'll send notes shortly.

63
00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.709
Thanks, everyone, this was really helpful.

64
00:02:15.059 --> 00:02:15.913
Part 1.

65
00:02:16.193 --> 00:02:17.793
Upgrade your vocabulary.

66
00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:20.387
Here is a quick table:

67
00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.181
Basic, and Professional.

68
00:02:22.461 --> 00:02:23.229
I think:

69
00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:25.771
In my view / My recommendation is.

70
00:02:26.051 --> 00:02:27.203
Very important:

71
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:29.253
Critical / High-priority.

72
00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:30.408
Problem:

73
00:02:30.688 --> 00:02:32.672
Issue / Challenge / Blocker.

74
00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:33.677
Fix:

75
00:02:33.957 --> 00:02:35.344
Resolve / Address.

76
00:02:35.624 --> 00:02:36.328
Big:

77
00:02:36.608 --> 00:02:38.443
Significant / Substantial.

78
00:02:38.723 --> 00:02:39.405
Check:

79
00:02:39.685 --> 00:02:41.136
Verify / Review.

80
00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:42.099
Tell:

81
00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:44.299
Inform / Update / Flag.

82
00:02:44.579 --> 00:02:45.368
Start:

83
00:02:45.648 --> 00:02:47.099
Kick off / Initiate.

84
00:02:48.449 --> 00:02:49.110
Get:

85
00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.819
Obtain / Receive.

86
00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:52.059
Do the needful:

87
00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:55.689
Please take care of this / Could you please specific action.

88
00:02:55.969 --> 00:02:56.907
Revert back:

89
00:02:57.187 --> 00:02:58.851
Reply / Get back to me.

90
00:02:59.131 --> 00:02:59.985
Prepone:

91
00:03:00.265 --> 00:03:02.099
Move earlier / Bring forward.

92
00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:03.403
Kindly do it:

93
00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.750
Could you please...

94
00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.993
Same to you (for Have a good day):

95
00:03:07.273 --> 00:03:08.361
Thanks, you too!

96
00:03:09.711 --> 00:03:10.351
Tip:

97
00:03:10.631 --> 00:03:13.809
Common Indian-English phrases to swap in global teams.

98
00:03:14.089 --> 00:03:22.175
Do the needful, revert back, prepone, out of station, pass out (graduate) are understood in India but can confuse global colleagues.

99
00:03:22.455 --> 00:03:24.375
Use the professional column above.

100
00:03:25.725 --> 00:03:27.261
That's the end of this lesson.

101
00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:32.191
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

102
00:03:32.471 --> 00:03:38.594
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

